# Capture Profile Data (Version 2.x) > Anonymous and Known Users

In the Data 360 Module, all customers are considered known by default. To mark a customer as anonymous, set the `isAnonymous` profile attribute to `"1"`. Setting `isAnonymous` to `"0"` ensures customers are considered known.

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"swift", "title": "iOS", "src": "" }
import Cdp
import SFMCSDK

...

// treat a profile as anonymous
SFMCSdk.identity.setProfileAttributes([.cdp: ["isAnonymous": "1"]])
// or use this convenience function
CdpModule.shared.setProfileToAnonymous()

// treat a profile as known
SFMCSdk.identity.setProfileAttributes([.cdp: ["isAnonymous": "0"]])
// or use this convenience function
CdpModule.shared.setProfileToKnown()
```

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"kotlin", "title": "Android", "src": "" }
// treat a profile as anonymous
SFMCSdk.requestSdk { sdk ->
  sdk.identity.setProfileAttribute("isAnonymous", "1", CDP)
}

// treat a profile as known
SFMCSdk.requestSdk { sdk ->
  sdk.identity.setProfileAttribute("isAnonymous", "0", CDP)
}
```

# Capture Engagement Data (Version 3.x) > Implementation Examples

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"swift", "title": "iOS", "src": "" }
import Cdp
import SFMCSDK

...

// Add to cart
