# Consent Management (Version 3.x) > Grant or Revoke Consent

The Data 360 Module can't transmit events from a mobile device to Data 360 until the mobile application has collected customer consent for data collection.

If no prior consent has been set, then the initial state is pending. See the consent states table for platform-specific behavior during the pending state. If consent is granted, events begin transmitting to Data 360 (on Android, any queued events are flushed). If revoked, any queued events are deleted.

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"swift", "title": "iOS", "src": "" }
import Cdp

// when a user consents to data collection — property style
CdpModule.shared.consent = .optIn

// when a user does not consent to data collection — property style
CdpModule.shared.consent = .optOut

// method style (equivalent; also Objective-C compatible)
CdpModule.shared.setConsent(consent: .optIn)
```

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"kotlin", "title": "Android", "src": "" }
import com.salesforce.marketingcloud.cdp.CdpSdk
import com.salesforce.marketingcloud.cdp.consent.Consent

// when a user consents to data collection
CdpSdk.requestSdk { sdk -> sdk.consent = Consent.OPT_IN }

// when a user does not consent to data collection
CdpSdk.requestSdk { sdk -> sdk.consent = Consent.OPT_OUT }

// Consent.PENDING cannot be set manually — attempting to assign it
// throws an IllegalArgumentException
```

