# Consent Management (Version 2.x) > Grant or Revoke Consent

The Data 360 Module can't transmit events from a mobile device to Data 360 until the mobile application has collected customer consent for data collection.

If no prior consent has been set, then the initial state is pending. In this state, events are queued locally until consent is granted or revoked. If consent is granted, the queued events are transmitted to Data 360. If revoked, they're deleted from the queue.

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"swift", "title": "iOS", "src": "" }
import Cdp

// when a user consents to data collection
CdpModule.shared.setConsent(consent: Consent.optIn)

// when a user does not consent to data collection
CdpModule.shared.setConsent(consent: Consent.optOut)
```

