# Initialization (Version 3.x) > iOS Example

```swift
import Cdp
import SFMCSDK

...

let appId = "{appIdFromMobileConnector}"
let endpoint = "https://{endpointFromMobileConnector}"

// 1. (Optional) Enable logging. In this example, the logger is set to show debug messages and higher.

SFMCSdk.setLogger(logLevel: .debug)

// 2. Configure the Data 360 Module

let cdpConfig = CdpConfigBuilder(
    appId: appId,
    endpoint: endpoint
)
    .trackScreens(false)
    .trackLifecycle(false)
    .sessionTimeout(600)
    .eventFlushRate(EventFlushRateQuantityAndInterval(quantity: 10, interval: 30.0)) // Optional (3.0.2+)
    .build()

// 3. Initialize the Engagement Mobile SDK with the Data 360 Module registered

let sdkConfig = ConfigBuilder().setCdp(config: cdpConfig).build()
SFMCSdk.initializeSdk(sdkConfig) { status in
    for moduleStatus in status where moduleStatus.moduleName == ModuleName.cdp {
        if moduleStatus.initStatus == .success {
            // SDK is ready
            print(CdpModule.shared.state)
        }
    }
}
```

The `SFMCSdk.initializeSdk(_:completionHandler:)` method calls the handler once per registered module with its initialization status. Filter by `moduleName == ModuleName.cdp` to act only on the Data 360 Module result. A status of `initStatus == .success` means the module is ready to use.

# Location Tracking (Version 2.x) > Location Tracking (Version 2.x)

The Data 360 Module for the Engagement Mobile SDK supports location tracking for all events. Enable this functionality using the `setLocation` method on the Data 360 Module to set `coordinates` and `expiresIn`.

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"swift", "title": "iOS", "src": "" }
// Prepare the coordinates using the CdpCoordinates wrapper
let coordinates = CdpCoordinates(latitude: 54.187738, longitude: 15.554440)

// Set the location coordinates and expiration time in seconds
CdpModule.shared.setLocation(coordinates: coordinates, expiresIn: 60)
```

```sfdocs-code {"lang":"kotlin", "title": "Android", "src": "" }
CdpSdk.requestSdk { sdk ->
    // Prepare the coordinates using the Coordinates wrapper
    val coordinates = Coordinates(latitude = 54.187738, longitude = 15.554440)

    // Set the location coordinates and expiration time in seconds
    sdk.setLocation(coordinates = coordinates, expiresIn = 60)
}
```

When the SDK has non-expired location coordinates, the location attributes are automatically appended to event attributes as key-value pairs with the key names `latitude` and `longitude`.

When the expiration interval is exceeded, the SDK location coordinates are cleared and no longer attached to events. To prevent location from being attached to events before the coordinates expire, call `setLocation` and pass `nil` values as the coordinates.

:::note
You're responsible for handling location tracking permission from the customer, requesting location permission, fetching the location, and ensuring the desired accuracy range.
:::

