# Account Data > Capture Account Data Using the Sitemap

To inject the `account.id` into all interaction events across your site consistently, use the Sitemap's `onActionEvent` global handler.

This example assumes the `accountId` is already available on the page, such as being stored in a global JavaScript variable like `window.accountId`.

```javascript
SalesforceInteractions.init().then(() => {
  const sitemapConfig = {
    global: {
      // The onActionEvent function runs immediately before any event is sent.
      onActionEvent: (event) => {
        const accountId = window.accountId; // Get the ID from your site's variable

        if (accountId) {
          // Inject the account ID into the event object
          event.account = event.account || {};
          event.account.id = accountId;
        }
        return event; // Always return the modified event
      },
    },
    pageTypes: [
      // Example of a page type definition that fires an interaction
      {
        name: "product_detail",
        isMatch: () => true, // Example simple matching rule
        interaction: {
          name: SalesforceInteractions.InteractionName.ViewCatalogObject,
          catalogObject: {
            type: "Product",
            id: "product-xyz",
            attributes: {
              name: "Product XYZ",
              category: "Clothing",
              color: "Red",
            },
          },
        },
      },
    ],
  };
  SalesforceInteractions.initSitemap(sitemapConfig);
});
```

